From 55d8cf2c6946b7f22c9b98dac6d15114f5949848 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jefferson-Butler1 <jefferson.butler@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:30:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(server): an agent's self-snooze survives its own turn
 completing

A run that completes after a snooze wakes the thread, so an agent that
snoozed its own thread mid-turn was woken by finishing that same turn.
Self-snooze now waits for the active run to complete, like self-settle,
returning snoozesWhenTurnEnds. A failed or interrupted run, a snooze
someone else set meanwhile, or a passed wake time leaves the thread awake.

Refs #18985
